  <p>
  <strong >Xingyu Li</strong> <span class="research-intro-chinese-name" lang="zh-Hans">李星谕</span> (She/her) is a design researcher and artist pursuing her fourth-year-PhD in Georgia Tech’s
  <a href="https://dm.lmc.gatech.edu/"> Digital Media</a> program. 
  Her research explores how art and design create conditions for people to shape what ethics means through embodied and affective encounters with technology. 
  She creates spaces where people can explore their relationships with technology, reflect on their experiences, and share their thoughts and feelings.</p>
  <p>
  Xingyu Li's work in HCI is situated in design research and informed by postphenomenology and feminist epistemology. 
  She combines aesthetic inquiry and socially engaged art with qualitative research methods, often working through community workshops and art exhibitions.
  </p>
  </ResearchIntro>
